
  - [38;5;153mREADME.md:3-5[39m names the consumers: the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and later), and the nightly partner export.
  - It also states the policy: "Field names in the response are part of the contract; changes go through a versioned
    endpoint."

  The iOS app and the partner export are the sharp edge — you can't redeploy either in lockstep with the API, so
  shipping the rename alone breaks them until they're updated. The internal [38;5;153mu.id[39m source field and [38;5;153m/orders[39m are
  unaffected; only the JSON key changes.

